# Forever LAN — Guardrails

- This is a **one-weekend LAN product**, not a SaaS platform.
- **One weekend / one dataset / no historical runs.** No multi-weekend history, accounts, cloud analytics, or persistent player profiles.
- Do **not** introduce accounts, cloud services, multi-run history, background infrastructure, WAN tunnels, or a separate analytics database unless the host explicitly requests them.
- Prefer **rebuilding views from the existing event dataset** over creating new persistence layers.
- Preserve **original event timestamps** (`ev.ts`) and **Friday → Saturday offline catch-up** (backlog first, then live). Do not assume the host is online all weekend.
- **Friend discovery must never gate local collection.** Collect + queue while offline; discover/reconnect + flush when the host is up.
- Prefer **simple derived calculations** over speculative metrics.
- Never invent unavailable WoW data such as XP/hour or hidden power stats.
- Keep the three-level honesty model visible where it matters: **Logged / Counted / Guessed** (internal: Observed / Derived / Inferred) — never present counted/guessed as raw logs.
- Separate **observed telemetry** from **derived analytics** (Hall awards, pace, streaks, etc.).
- Optimize for a **fun, readable control-room experience** (ESPN + Strava + Mario Party / WoW flavor) — not enterprise analytics.

## UI requirements

- **Live:** primary control-room; at a glance who is ahead, catching up, what just happened, who is dying, what needs attention — no burying the important stuff.
- **Wrap:** Hall of Shame/Fame near the top / above the fold.

